*> Implementation test (002-lane-mobsfull-h11; docs/protocol/20 section 6.1 Creeper, 6.2 Explosion): ignition by an item of the creeper_igniters tag (flint_and_steel,
*> fire_charge: ignited, the flint takes 1 durability, the charge is used up; any other item does nothing), an ignited creeper swells with no target and explodes at
*> the fuse 30; a landing adds floor(fall distance x 1.5) to the swell, at most maxSwell - 5 = 25 (the creeper's causeFallDamage); the swell needs line of sight to
*> the target; AvoidEntityGoal cat and ocelot within 6 blocks (box 6, 3, 6) at speed 1.0, 1.2 within 7 blocks; a powered creeper's kill gives one head by the victim
*> type (zombie, creeper, skeleton; piglin and wither skeleton have no row here), once per explosion. The lingering cloud needs the area effect cloud entity (open).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-MOB-20-6-2.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY BRWORLD.
 COPY STDMOBS.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-KEY24               PIC X(24).
 01 WS-ENTITY-ROW          PIC X(66).
 01 WS-ITEM-ROW            PIC X(270).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ITEM-ID             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-M                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CREEPER             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OCELOT              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VICTIM              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID-A                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HAND0               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-SNEAK0              BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-PX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PY                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X0                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z0                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SIZE                BINARY-LONG VALUE 9.
 01 WS-FY                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KIND                BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STOP                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HX                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-HZ                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-AVOID               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DROPPED             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WANT-KEY            PIC X(24).
 01 WS-FOUND               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FALL                FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-POWER               FLOAT-LONG VALUE 6.
 01 WS-DESTROY             BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-NO-FIRE             BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-SRC                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "MS-TEST-OPEN" USING WS-PLAYER
     MOVE PL-CONN(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-CONN
     MOVE PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-DIM
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     COMPUTE WS-PX = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-X(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-PY = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Y(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-PZ = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Z(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-X0 = WS-PX - 4
     COMPUTE WS-Z0 = WS-PZ - 4
     COMPUTE WS-FY = WS-PY + 60
     CALL "MS-TEST-FLOOR" USING WS-DIM WS-X0 WS-Z0 WS-SIZE WS-FY WS-KIND
     MOVE "creeper" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     CALL "STDMOB-INDEX" USING WS-TYPE WS-M
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-PX + 1.5
     COMPUTE WS-Y = PL-Y(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Z
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-CREEPER
     MOVE EN-ID(WS-CREEPER) TO WS-ID-A

*>   Ignition.
     MOVE "stick" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM GIVE-HELD-1
     CALL "TEST-INTERACT" USING WS-CONN WS-ID-A WS-HAND0 WS-SNEAK0
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a stick does not ignite it" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "flint_and_steel" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM GIVE-HELD-1
     CALL "TEST-INTERACT" USING WS-CONN WS-ID-A WS-HAND0 WS-SNEAK0
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: flint and steel ignites it, the item stays" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 1 * 10 + 1
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER) * 10 + PL-SLOT-COUNT(WS-PLAYER, 1)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE "fire_charge" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM GIVE-HELD-1
     MOVE 2 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(WS-PLAYER, 1)
     CALL "TEST-INTERACT" USING WS-CONN WS-ID-A WS-HAND0 WS-SNEAK0
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a fire charge ignites it and is used up" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 1 * 10 + 1
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER) * 10 + PL-SLOT-COUNT(WS-PLAYER, 1)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   An ignited creeper far from everyone swells to the fuse and explodes.
     COMPUTE EN-X(WS-CREEPER) = WS-PX + 40
     MOVE 0 TO EN-TARGET(WS-CREEPER) EN-TARGET-ID(WS-CREEPER) EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) EN-SWELL-DIR(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE 1 TO EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 10
         CALL "STDMOB-SWELL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-STOP
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: ignited, it swells by 1 a tick with no target" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 10 * 10 + 1
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) * 10 + WS-STOP
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 19
         CALL "STDMOB-SWELL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-STOP
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: at swell 29 it still stands" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 1 * 10 + 1
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-USED(WS-CREEPER) * 10 + WS-STOP
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "STDMOB-SWELL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-STOP
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: at the fuse 30 it explodes and is gone" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 0 * 10 + 2
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-USED(WS-CREEPER) * 10 + WS-STOP
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Fall: a creeper dropping 6 blocks onto the floor swells by floor(fall x 1.5) at most 25.
     MOVE "creeper" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-PX + 0.5
     COMPUTE WS-Y = WS-FY + 7
     COMPUTE WS-Z = WS-PZ + 0.5
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-CREEPER
     MOVE 0 TO EN-ON-GROUND(WS-CREEPER) EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 60 OR EN-ON-GROUND(WS-CREEPER) = 1
         CALL "STDMOB-STEP" USING WS-CREEPER
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a landing from 6 blocks adds floor(1.5 x fall) to the swell (9 to 11)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) >= 9 AND EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) <= 11
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 3.5 TO WS-FALL
     MOVE 0 TO EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER)
     CALL "STDMOB-CREEPER-FALL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-FALL
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a fall of 3.5 adds floor(5.25) = 5" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 5 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 40 TO WS-FALL
     CALL "STDMOB-CREEPER-FALL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-FALL
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: the swell from a fall is at most maxSwell - 5 = 25" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 25 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 29 TO EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FALL
     CALL "STDMOB-CREEPER-FALL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-FALL
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a swell above 25 is cut back to 25 by a landing" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 25 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Line of sight: swell 5 with the target 3 blocks above, first in the open, then under a roof.
     COMPUTE EN-X(WS-CREEPER) = WS-PX + 0.5
     COMPUTE EN-Y(WS-CREEPER) = WS-FY + 1
     COMPUTE EN-Z(WS-CREEPER) = WS-PZ + 0.5
     MOVE 0 TO EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE WS-PLAYER TO EN-TARGET(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE PL-ENTITY-ID(WS-PLAYER) TO EN-TARGET-ID(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE EN-X(WS-CREEPER) TO PL-X(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE EN-Z(WS-CREEPER) TO PL-Z(WS-PLAYER)
     COMPUTE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) = WS-FY + 1 + 2.5
     MOVE 5 TO EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-SWELL-DIR(WS-CREEPER)
     CALL "STDMOB-SWELL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-STOP
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: with the target in sight the swell grows" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 6 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     COMPUTE WS-FY = WS-FY + 3
     CALL "MS-TEST-FLOOR" USING WS-DIM WS-X0 WS-Z0 WS-SIZE WS-FY WS-KIND
     COMPUTE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) = WS-FY + 1
     CALL "STDMOB-SWELL" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-STOP
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: with a roof between, the swell shrinks" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 5 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-SWELL(WS-CREEPER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-CREEPER

*>   Avoiding cats and ocelots.
     COMPUTE WS-FY = WS-PY + 60
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-PX + 0.5
     COMPUTE WS-Y = WS-FY + 1
     COMPUTE WS-Z = WS-PZ + 0.5
     MOVE "creeper" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-CREEPER
     CALL "STDMOB-AVOID" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-HX WS-HZ WS-AVOID
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: with no cat near it does not avoid" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AVOID TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "cat" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-PX + 3.5
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-CAT
     CALL "STDMOB-AVOID" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-HX WS-HZ WS-AVOID
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a cat 3 blocks east: it walks west at 1.2 x 0.138" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 1 * 1000000 + 165600
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = WS-AVOID * 1000000 - WS-HX * 1000000
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: no north-south walk when the cat is due east" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = WS-HZ * 1000
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     COMPUTE EN-X(WS-CAT) = WS-PX + 6.6
     CALL "STDMOB-AVOID" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-HX WS-HZ WS-AVOID
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a cat 6.1 blocks away is outside the box 6" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AVOID TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     COMPUTE EN-X(WS-CAT) = WS-PX + 3.5
     COMPUTE EN-Y(WS-CAT) = WS-FY + 5
     CALL "STDMOB-AVOID" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-HX WS-HZ WS-AVOID
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a cat 4 blocks higher is outside the box 3" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AVOID TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     COMPUTE EN-Y(WS-CAT) = WS-FY + 1
     MOVE "ocelot" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-PX - 1.5
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-OCELOT
     CALL "STDMOB-AVOID" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-HX WS-HZ WS-AVOID
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: an ocelot 2 blocks west is nearer than the cat: it walks east" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-AVOID = 1 AND WS-HX > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE EN-X(WS-CREEPER) TO WS-HX
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-OCELOT
     CALL "STDMOB-STEP" USING WS-CREEPER
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: the step walks it away from the cat (west)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-X(WS-CREEPER) < WS-HX - 0.1
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-HEALTH(WS-CAT)
     CALL "STDMOB-AVOID" USING WS-CREEPER WS-M WS-HX WS-HZ WS-AVOID
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: dead cats are not avoided" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AVOID TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-CAT

*>   Charged-creeper heads.
     MOVE 1 TO EN-VARIANT(WS-CREEPER)
     MOVE "zombie" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-VICTIM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DROPPED
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VARIANT(WS-CREEPER)
     CALL "STDMOB-CHARGED-HEAD" USING WS-CREEPER WS-VICTIM WS-DROPPED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a plain creeper's kill gives no head" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DROPPED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO EN-VARIANT(WS-CREEPER)
     CALL "STDMOB-CHARGED-HEAD" USING WS-CREEPER WS-VICTIM WS-DROPPED
     MOVE "zombie_head" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM COUNT-ITEMS
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a powered creeper's zombie kill drops a zombie head" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 1 * 10 + 1
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-DROPPED * 10 + WS-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "STDMOB-CHARGED-HEAD" USING WS-CREEPER WS-VICTIM WS-DROPPED
     PERFORM COUNT-ITEMS
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: the head drops once per creeper" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-N TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-VICTIM
     MOVE "creeper" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-VICTIM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DROPPED
     CALL "STDMOB-CHARGED-HEAD" USING WS-CREEPER WS-VICTIM WS-DROPPED
     MOVE "creeper_head" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM COUNT-ITEMS
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a creeper victim drops a creeper head" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 1 * 10 + 1
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-DROPPED * 10 + WS-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-VICTIM
     MOVE "skeleton" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-VICTIM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DROPPED
     CALL "STDMOB-CHARGED-HEAD" USING WS-CREEPER WS-VICTIM WS-DROPPED
     MOVE "skeleton_skull" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM COUNT-ITEMS
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a skeleton victim drops a skeleton skull" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 1 * 10 + 1
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-DROPPED * 10 + WS-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-VICTIM
     MOVE "cow" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-VICTIM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DROPPED
     CALL "STDMOB-CHARGED-HEAD" USING WS-CREEPER WS-VICTIM WS-DROPPED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a cow has no head to drop" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DROPPED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-VICTIM
*>   A row-less victim: the bat has a row since lane p49f, so the entity is a ground item (the type "item" has no mob row).
     MOVE "cow" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-VICTIM
     MOVE "item" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     MOVE WS-TYPE TO EN-TYPE(WS-VICTIM)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DROPPED
     CALL "STDMOB-CHARGED-HEAD" USING WS-CREEPER WS-VICTIM WS-DROPPED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a type with no row gives no head" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DROPPED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-VICTIM
*>   A powered and ignited creeper sends both metadata entries.
     MOVE 1 TO EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER)
     CALL "STDMOB-VARIANT-SEND" USING WS-CREEPER
     MOVE 0 TO EN-IGNITED(WS-CREEPER)
*>   The explosion itself: a powered creeper kills a zombie next to it and a head lies there.
     MOVE "zombie" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM FIND-TYPE
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-PX + 1.5
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-VICTIM
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-PX + 0.5
     MOVE "zombie_head" TO WS-WANT-KEY
     PERFORM COUNT-ITEMS
     MOVE WS-N TO WS-I
     MOVE WS-CREEPER TO WS-SRC
     CALL "EXPLODE-RUN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-POWER WS-DESTROY WS-SRC WS-NO-FIRE
     PERFORM COUNT-ITEMS
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a powered blast that kills a zombie leaves one more zombie head" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = WS-I + 1
     MOVE WS-N TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 FIND-TYPE.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     STRING "minecraft:" DELIMITED BY SIZE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-WANT-KEY) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS.
 GIVE-HELD-1.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     STRING "minecraft:" DELIMITED BY SIZE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-WANT-KEY) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ITEM-ID WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-ITEM-ID TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(WS-PLAYER, 1)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(WS-PLAYER, 1)
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-VAR(WS-PLAYER, 1)
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HELD(WS-PLAYER).
 COUNT-ITEMS.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     STRING "minecraft:" DELIMITED BY SIZE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-WANT-KEY) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ITEM-ID WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM VARYING WS-FOUND FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-FOUND > EN-COUNT
         IF EN-USED(WS-FOUND) = 1 AND EN-ITEM(WS-FOUND) = WS-ITEM-ID AND EN-ITEM-COUNT(WS-FOUND) > 0
             ADD EN-ITEM-COUNT(WS-FOUND) TO WS-N
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM.
 END PROGRAM TEST-MOB-20-6-2.
 COPY CORETEST.
 COPY MOBSPTEST.
